explanation:
Section 53(1) of the IBC lays down the waterfall mechanism for distribution of proceeds:
(a) Firstly: the insolvency resolution process costs and the liquidation costs paid in full;
(b) Secondly: (i) workmen’s dues for the period of 24 months preceding the liquidation commencement date; and (ii) debts owed to a secured creditor in the event such secured creditor has relinquished security in the manner set out in section 52 (both rank pari passu);
(f) Further down the order: Government dues.
Therefore, the correct sequence puts liquidation costs first, followed jointly by workmen dues (24 months) and relinquished secured creditor debts pari passu, before government dues.
